      "gap": "Partial: (1) EiterGottlob manuscript p. 10: 'a hypothesis plays the role of what in other models is called an abducible proposition (see [14])', [14] being Console, Theseider Dupre and Torasso, 'On the Relationship Between Abduction and Deduction' (J. Logic Comput. 1991); finite-abduction.tex lines 26-27 say only 'also called the abducible atoms', dropping the attribution to other models and its reference, although the entry reports the source's other references (lines 52-54). (2) p. 10: the source argues that positive-atom hypotheses lose no generality by one construction: add x<->F to T, where x is a new variable added to the hypotheses H (new hypothesis set H with x added). Lines 54-60 report it and state that thm:p15-w02c-p15-027-formula-hypotheses 'proves this', but that theorem (lines 230-258; annex lines 288-335) proves a different construction in which every permitted hypothesis is replaced by a fresh atom (H' = {x_phi : phi in Phi}); the solution correspondence for the source's own construction, which keeps the atoms of H and adds x, is not written. Owed: supply the attribution with its locator and a written proof for the source's construction (or state and prove it as a case)."
